Regarding `-j`, currently it's a bit annoying that hashcat count words every time when `-j` is used, even when there isn't any reject rule specified.

I have an attack (-a 0) that runs for 6 hours (sha512crypt), so there is no way I can use any rule file with a big wordlist. So, instead of using a rule file, I constructed a single rule that I have specified in `-j` parameter. Now every start of hashcat takes appox. 20-30 min since hashcat counts words in my wordlist. But it doesn't make any sense since the amount of words is always the same. 

@davidbolvansky I haven't properly checked, but it seems like the case with reject rules in `-j` parameter is not covered in the current PR code.
